{
  "name": "Form of the Beast",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your bestial spark manifests in the form of natural weapons.</p><p>Choose one of the following options: bite, claws, horns, hooves, pincers, or tail. You permanently gain the selected option as a natural weapon. It deals 1d8 damage on a hit. You can choose whether it deals bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage when you select it. It counts as a simple weapon for you and you use your Strength modifier for attack and damage rolls with it.</p><p>You can choose how the natural weapon looks exactly. For example, the bite option might give you long fangs, mandibles, or even a beak.</p>",
